pe": "name", "content": "groove"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a long narrow cut"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He cuts a deep groove into the tree."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le06ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bark"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the outside of a tree"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The tree bark is rough and hard."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le06ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rubber"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an elastic waterproof substance "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Her rubber boots keep her dry in the rain."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le06ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to flow"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to move like water "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Rubber sap flows out of the tree."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le06ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "easily "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "without difficulty "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sap comes out easily."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le06ob09aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le06ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Present Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present</span> tense to talk about habits and routines.<br />These are things that you do frequently or every day."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I cut grooves into the bark to let the latex flow. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I tap the trees to get the latex."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look on the internet for an interesting job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out what the person does in their job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 30 to 40 words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use infinitives of purpose."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the Simple Present tense for routines."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I do research on an interesting job. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about what a person does at that job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I express purpose in connection with the job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe the job routines."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn4le06ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn4le06ob09re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn4le06ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Miguel</span>: I'm a rubber tapper. I tap trees in the rainforest. My day begins early. I tap the trees to get the latex, or natural rubber. It flows freely in the cool morning air.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: How do you collect the latex?", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn4le06ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Miguel</span>: I cut grooves into the bark to let the latex flow. Then, I attach a small cup to the tree to catch it. I tap 350 trees a day.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Do many people tap trees?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miguel</span>: No, not many people tap trees now. The rainforest is disappearing. The number of rubber trees is small. My children go to school to learn other skills.", "id": 2, "time": "16